1920,1036\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"Paul McCartney – Twickenham Film Studios, 16 January 1969\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690116-get-back_08-960x518.jpg\"></a></div></figure><figure class=\"gallery-item\"><div class=\"gallery-icon landscape\">\n<a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1969-photos/690116-get-back_09/\"><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIyMDAiIGhlaWdodD0iMTA4IiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMjAwIDEwOCI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"200\" height=\"108\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690116-get-back_09-200x108.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"Glyn Johns – Twickenham Film Studios, 16 January 1969\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690116-get-back_09-200x108.jpg 200w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690116-get-back_09-580x313.jpg 580w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690116-get-back_09-960x518.jpg 960w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690116-get-back_09-768x414.jpg 768w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690116-get-back_09-1536x829.jpg 1536w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690116-get-back_09-300x160.jpg 300w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690116-get-back_09.jpg 1920w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\" data-attachment-id=\"101423\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1969-photos/690116-get-back_09/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690116-get-back_09.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"1920,1036\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"Glyn Johns – Twickenham Film Studios, 16 January 1969\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690116-get-back_09-960x518.jpg\"></a></div></figure><figure class=\"gallery-item\"><div class=\"gallery-icon landscape\">\n<a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1969-photos/690116-get-back_10/\"><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIyMDAiIGhlaWdodD0iMTA4IiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMjAwIDEwOCI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"200\" height=\"108\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690116-get-back_10-200x108.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"Paul McCartney – Twickenham Film Studios, 16 January 1969\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690116-get-back_10-200x108.jpg 200w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690116-get-back_10-580x313.jpg 580w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690116-get-back_10-960x518.jpg 960w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690116-get-back_10-768x414.jpg 768w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690116-get-back_10-1536x829.jpg 1536w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690116-get-back_10-300x160.jpg 300w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690116-get-back_10.jpg 1920w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\" data-attachment-id=\"101424\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1969-photos/690116-get-back_10/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690116-get-back_10.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"1920,1036\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"Paul McCartney – Twickenham Film Studios, 16 January 1969\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690116-get-back_10-960x518.jpg\"></a></div></figure></div><p>After the completion of McCartney’s demo, George Harrison arrived at Twickenham to meet Glyn Johns. The pair travelled to Apple Corps’ headquarters at 3 Savile Row, London, to inspect the recording studio <a href=\"/people/alexis-mardas/\">Alexis ‘Magic Alex’ Mardas</a> had been constructing in the basement.</p><p>They found the facilities substandard, with unacceptable levels of distortion and hiss, and realised they would be unable to proceed with The Beatles’ project without new equipment. Johns contacted <a href=\"/people/george-martin/\">George Martin</a> with an urgent request for replacement gear, which EMI agreed to lend to Apple.</p><blockquote><div>The mixing console [made by Mardas] was made of bit of wood and an old oscilloscope. It looked like the control panel of a B-52 bomber. They actually tried a session on this desk, they did a take, but when they played back the tape it was all hum and hiss. Terrible. The Beatles walked out, that was the end of it.</div></blockquote><div class=\"source\">Dave Harries, recording engineer<br>\n<a href=\"https://geni.us/lewisohnsessions\" target=\"_blank\"><em>The Complete Beatles Recording Sessions</em></a>, Mark Lewisohn</div><div data-carousel-extra=\"{&quot;blog_id&quot;:1,&quot;permalink&quot;:&quot;https://www.beatlesbible.com/1969/01/16/get-back-let-it-be-sessions-day-10/&quot;}\" id=\"gallery-3\" class=\"gallery galleryid-101409 gallery-columns-3 gallery-size-thumbnail\"><figure class=\"gallery-item\"><div class=\"gallery-icon landscape\">\n<a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1969-photos/690116-get-back_16/\"><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIyMDAiIGhlaWdodD0iMTA4IiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMjAwIDEwOCI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"200\" height=\"108\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690116-get-back_16-200x108.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"George Harrison – Twickenham Film Studios, 16 January 1969\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690116-get-back_16-200x108.jpg 200w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690116-get-back_16-580x313.jpg 580w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690116-get-back_16-960x518.jpg 960w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690116-get-back_16-768x414.jpg 768w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690116-get-back_16-1536x829.jpg 1536w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690116-get-back_16-300x160.jpg 300w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690116-get-back_16.jpg 1920w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\" data-attachment-id=\"101460\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1969-photos/690116-get-back_16/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690116-get-back_16.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"1920,1036\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"George Harrison – Twickenham Film Studios, 16 January 1969\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690116-get-back_16-960x518.jpg\"></a></div></figure><figure class=\"gallery-item\"><div class=\"gallery-icon landscape\">\n<a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1969-photos/690116-get-back_17/\"><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIyMDAiIGhlaWdodD0iMTA4IiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMjAwIDEwOCI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"200\" height=\"108\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690116-get-back_17-200x108.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"George Harrison – Twickenham Film Studios, 16 January 1969\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690116-get-back_17-200x108.jpg 200w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690116-get-back_17-580x313.jpg 580w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690116-get-back_17-960x518.jpg 960w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690116-get-back_17-768x414.jpg 768w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690116-get-back_17-1536x829.jpg 1536w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690116-get-back_17-300x160.jpg 300w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690116-get-back_17.jpg 1920w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\" data-attachment-id=\"101461\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1969-photos/690116-get-back_17/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690116-get-back_17.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"1920,1036\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"George Harrison – Twickenham Film Studios, 16 January 1969\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690116-get-back_17-960x518.jpg\"></a></div></figure><figure class=\"gallery-item\"><div class=\"gallery-icon landscape\">\n<a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1969-photos/690116-get-back_18/\"><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIyMDAiIGhlaWdodD0iMTA4IiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMjAwIDEwOCI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"200\" height=\"108\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690116-get-back_18-200x108.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"Recording colsole – Apple Studios, 16 January 1969\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690116-get-back_18-200x108.jpg 200w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690116-get-back_18-580x313.jpg 580w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690116-get-back_18-960x518.jpg 960w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690116-get-back_18-768x414.jpg 768w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690116-get-back_18-1536x829.jpg 1536w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690116-get-back_18-300x160.jpg 300w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690116-get-back_18.jpg 1920w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\" data-attachment-id=\"101462\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1969-photos/690116-get-back_18/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690116-get-back_18.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"1920,1036\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"Recording colsole – Apple Studios, 16 January 1969\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690116-get-back_18-960x518.jpg\"></a></div></figure></div><p>Mardas later defended his position, saying the equipment was still in a prototype stage and unfit for recording purposes.</p><blockquote><div>The metal was an eighth of an inch out around the knobs and switches. It had obviously been done with a hammer and chisel instead of being properly designed and machined. It did pass signals but Glyn Johns said ‘I can’t do anything with this. I can’t make a record with this board’.</div></blockquote><div class=\"source\">Alan Parsons, tape operator<br>\n<a href=\"https://geni.us/lewisohnsessions\" target=\"_blank\"><em>The Complete Beatles Recording Sessions</em></a>, Mark Lewisohn</div><p>The equipment was installed by Dave Harries and Keith Slaughter, plus engineers from EMI, who worked through the weekend to make the studio suitable for The Beatles. They connected two portable four-track mixing consoles, which fed sound into Harrison’s eight-track 3M tape machine.</p><blockquote><div>The mixing console was sold as scrap to a secondhand electronics shop in the Edgware Road for £5. It wasn’t worth any more.</div></blockquote><div class=\"source\"><a href=\"/people/geoff-emerick/\">Geoff Emerick</a><br>\n<a href=\"https://geni.us/lewisohnsessions\" target=\"_blank\"><em>The Complete Beatles Recording Sessions</em></a>, Mark Lewisohn</div>\n<!--[googlesitekit-end-of-content]--><div style=\"font-size: 12px; margin: 10px 0 10px 0;\"><strong>Page last updated:</strong> 7 January 2022</div></div></div><div class=\"on-this-day-wrapper\"><h3>Also on this day...</h3><ul><li>2021: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/2021/01/16/phil-spector-dies/\">Phil Spector dies</a></li><li>1990: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1990/01/16/paul-mccartney-live-wembley-arena-london-4/\">Paul McCartney live: Wembley Arena, London</a></li><li>1981: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1981/01/16/uk-single-release-woman-john-lennon/\">UK single release: Woman by John Lennon</a></li><li>1980: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1980/01/16/paul-mccartney-arrested-marijuana-possession-tokyo-japan/\">Paul McCartney is arrested in Japan for marijuana possession</a></li><li>1979: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1979/01/16/recording-mixing-daytime-nighttime-suffering-wings/\">Recording, mixing: Daytime Nighttime Suffering by Wings</a></li><li>1978: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1978/01/16/mixing-famous-groupies-morse-moose-and-the-grey-goose-wings/\">Mixing: Famous Groupies, Morse Moose And The Grey Goose by Wings</a></li><li>1976: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1976/01/16/recording-silly-love-songs-wings/\">Recording: Silly Love Songs by Wings</a></li><li>1975: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1975/01/16/travel-paul-mccartney-new-york-new-orleans/\">Travel: Paul McCartney – New York to New Orleans</a></li><li>1973: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1973/01/16/editing-hold-me-tight-lazy-dynamite-hands-of-love-power-cut-wings/\">Editing: Hold Me Tight/Lazy Dynamite/Hands Of Love/Power Cut by Wings</a></li><li>1970: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1970/01/16/john-lennon-bag-one-exhibition-raided-by-police/\">John Lennon’s Bag One exhibition is raided by police</a></li><li>1967: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1967/01/16/joe-orton-begins-writing-beatles-film-script-up-against-it/\">Joe Orton begins writing a script for The Beatles’ third film</a></li><li>1965: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1965/01/16/live-another-beatles-christmas-show-20/\">Live: Another Beatles Christmas Show</a></li><li>1964: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1964/01/16/beatles-reach-number-one-america/\">The Beatles reach number one in America</a></li><li>1964: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1964/01/16/live-olympia-theatre-paris/\">The Beatles live: Olympia Theatre, Paris</a></li><li>1963: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1963/01/16/radio-here-we-go-2/\">Radio: Here We Go</a></li><li>1963: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1963/01/16/television-people-and-places-4/\">Television: People And Places</a></li><li>1957: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1957/01/16/cavern-club-opens-mathew-street-liverpool/\">The Cavern Club opens in Mathew Street, Liverpool</a></li></ul><p>Want more? Visit the <a title=\"Day after day: the Beatles' history\" href=\"/history/\">Beatles history section</a>.</p></div>",
  "textContent": "The tenth day of the Get Back/Let It Be sessions was the final one at Twickenham Film Studios. The Beatles had decided to relocate to the basement studio at their Apple Corps headquarters at 3 Savile Row, London, a condition of George Harrison rejoining. Harrison had walked out of the band on 10 January 1969.\n\n\n\n\n\nOn this day, 16 January 1969, the set at Twickenham was dismantled by Mal Evans, Kevin Harrington, and Glyn Johns. The Beatles were not scheduled to attend, but Paul McCartney turned up to record a piano demo of the future Abbey Road song ‘Oh! Darling’.The demo recording, produced and engineered by Glyn Johns, was shown in Peter Jackson’s 2021 documentary Get Back.\n\n\n\n\n\nAfter the completion of McCartney’s demo, George Harrison arrived at Twickenham to meet Glyn Johns. The pair travelled to Apple Corps’ headquarters at 3 Savile Row, London, to inspect the recording studio Alexis ‘Magic Alex’ Mardas had been constructing in the basement.They found the facilities substandard, with unacceptable levels of distortion and hiss, and realised they would be unable to proceed with The Beatles’ project without new equipment. Johns contacted George Martin with an urgent request for replacement gear, which EMI agreed to lend to Apple.The mixing console [made by Mardas] was made of bit of wood and an old oscilloscope. It looked like the control panel of a B-52 bomber. They actually tried a session on this desk, they did a take, but when they played back the tape it was all hum and hiss. Terrible. The Beatles walked out, that was the end of it.Dave Harries, recording engineer\nThe Complete Beatles Recording Sessions, Mark Lewisohn\n\n\nMardas later defended his position, saying the equipment was still in a prototype stage and unfit for recording purposes.The metal was an eighth of an inch out around the knobs and switches. It had obviously been done with a hammer and chisel instead of being properly designed and machined. It did pass signals but Glyn Johns said ‘I can’t do anything with this. I can’t make a record with this board’.Alan Parsons, tape operator\nThe Complete Beatles Recording Sessions, Mark LewisohnThe equipment was installed by Dave Harries and Keith Slaughter, plus engineers from EMI, who worked through the weekend to make the studio suitable for The Beatles. They connected two portable four-track mixing consoles, which fed sound into Harrison’s eight-track 3M tape machine.The mixing console was sold as scrap to a secondhand electronics shop in the Edgware Road for £5. It wasn’t worth any more.Geoff Emerick\nThe Complete Beatles Recording Sessions, Mark Lewisohn\nPage last updated: 7 January 2022Also on this day...2021: Phil Spector dies1990: Paul McCartney live: Wembley Arena, London1981: UK single release: Woman by John Lennon1980: Paul McCartney is arrested in Japan for marijuana possession1979: Recording, mixing: Daytime Nighttime Suffering by Wings1978: Mixing: Famous Groupies, Morse Moose And The Grey Goose by Wings1976: Recording: Silly Love Songs by Wings1975: Travel: Paul McCartney – New York to New Orleans1973: Editing: Hold Me Tight/Lazy Dynamite/Hands Of Love/Power Cut by Wings1970: John Lennon’s Bag One exhibition is raided by police1967: Joe Orton begins writing a script for The Beatles’ third film1965: Live: Another Beatles Christmas Show1964: The Beatles reach number one in America1964: The Beatles live: Olympia Theatre, Paris1963: Radio: Here We Go1963: Television: People And Places1957: The Cavern Club opens in Mathew Street, LiverpoolWant more? Visit the Beatles history section.",
